STM32G4: start LPUART1 (backport of Betaflight PR #15723)

Betaflight 2026.6.2 sets up every UART with ST's LL_USART_Init(), which only
knows USART1-3 and UART4-5. For LPUART1 it finds no clock, returns an error,
and Betaflight leaves the port off without a message. On the T-Motor Pacer G4
Alpha HD, LPUART1 TX (PA2) is the ESC plugs' TLM line, so ESC Sensor on
LPUART1 receives nothing.

Upstream fixed this on master in PR #15723 (commit e29ff7245, 2026-09-22),
after 2026.6.2. This is that change unmodified: LPUART1 is initialised with
LL_LPUART_Init() and a prescaler chosen from the baud rate, and
stm32g4xx_ll_lpuart.c joins the G4 build. With it, ESC Sensor on LPUART1 in
half-duplex mode reads the Pacer's BLHeli_32 telemetry (tested 2026-11-12).
Drop this patch once the release in use includes #15723.

Applies to Betaflight 2026.6.2. From the root of the Betaflight source:

    patch -p1 < stm32g4-lpuart1-init.patch

